WEBVTT

00:26:28.472 --> 00:26:30.480
that it's easier to fix a biased algorithm

00:26:30.504 --> 00:26:32.293
than a biased human.

00:26:32.317 --> 00:26:35.242
So where does that leave us
on computer-driven hiring?

00:26:35.266 --> 00:26:40.170
CM: I would say that we're making this
a little too black and white.

00:26:40.194 --> 00:26:44.202
The real path forward is not
algorithm or clinical judgment,

00:26:44.226 --> 00:26:46.493
but its algorithm and clinical judgment.

00:26:46.517 --> 00:26:48.629
Let them, you know, make their judgments,

00:26:48.653 --> 00:26:50.289
reach the conclusion on their own,

00:26:50.313 --> 00:26:52.645
but let them know
what the model would say.

00:26:52.669 --> 00:26:55.980
AG: I'm still not a huge fan
of using algorithms to hire candidates,

00:26:56.004 --> 00:26:58.162
but I'll concede
that we might learn something

00:26:58.186 --> 00:27:01.717
from including their recommendations
as one input into our decisions.